  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), MFD1 seen from the front-left, screen with backing plate, mount on the right side; all OSBs, the four rockers and the BRT knob visible",
  "mappingSource": "WinWing MFD1 User Manual V1.4 (2024.02) section 2.2 \"Key positions\" drawing, page 10 (https://eu.winctrl.com/static/ipfs/QmPM5B75RK5UGNrmuc9CWAb2DtE4Gygtqu4aPGzVX4qUNv): left OSBs 1/3/5/7/9 top to bottom, bottom OSBs 12-20 even left to right, right OSBs 31/29/27/25/23 top to bottom, top OSBs 42/40/38/36/34 left to right, GAIN 10 up/11 down, CONT 22 up/21 down, SYM 33/32, DAY 43 / NGT 44, side thumbwheel 45/46/47, BRT knob Z 0-4095 and 48; catalog also cites the EDCD maps 4098BEE1/4098BEE2",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "panel.encoder.1 (KNOB, 48 press / 49 ccw / 50 cw) and panel.axis.1 (BRT, Z) are the same physical BRT knob; both markers sit on it with a small offset. The manual only shows 48 at the knob next to its OFF label (48 may be the OFF detent rather than a press); 49/50 come from the EDCD map only, so encoder.1 is map=medium. The side thumbwheel (manual 45 top / 46 / 47 bottom) sits on the left frame between NGT and the first left OSB; it is not visible at this angle (kept as a low candidate). Catalog says 47 = SIDE up, 45 = SIDE down, the manual drawing puts 45 at the top and 47 at the bottom (discrepancy already noted in the catalog). The narrow keys between the OSBs (2/4/6/8, 13-19 odd, 24-30 even, 35-41 odd) have no catalog parts.",
